This cannot be tested, since s_client does not send early_data
(although called with `-early_data` option), if server does not indicate it
supports early_data by early_data extension in `NewSessionTicket` message of
the first handshake. If server's context is set with
SSL_CTX_set_max_early_data, it will support early data and client starts
sending early_data. However, this is not desired feature for the server, since
62351-3 don't allow 0-RTT.

Make s_client to send early_data, although server does not support it.
